%% Implemented v0.2 focused slide-edit sequence.
sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    actor Client as CLI or TUI
    participant App as SfumatoApplication
    participant Config as EffectiveConfigResolver
    participant FS as WorkspaceFileSystem
    participant Deck as DeckDocument
    participant Prompt as PromptCatalog
    participant Agent as AgentRunner
    participant Render as Diagram and Slide renderers
    participant Tx as ArtifactTransaction

    Client->>App: edit_slides(command)
    App->>Config: resolve project and text model
    Config-->>App: EffectiveConfig
    App->>FS: canonicalize requested Markdown and project artifact root
    FS-->>App: contained managed revision path
    App->>FS: read deck and copy parent revision into staging
    App->>Deck: parse, validate, and snapshot
    Deck-->>App: revision-guarded ReviewSnapshot
    App->>Prompt: render edit pair with instruction and snapshot
    App->>Agent: request RFC 6902 patch
    opt provider context or output limit
        App->>Prompt: render compact edit pair
        App->>Agent: request compact patch
    end
    Agent-->>App: RFC 6902 patch
    App->>Deck: allow tests and content-only slide Markdown replacements
    opt first patch is invalid
        App->>Prompt: render corrective edit pair with validation error
        App->>Agent: request one corrected patch
        Agent-->>App: corrected RFC 6902 patch
        App->>Deck: apply and validate
    end
    App->>Render: inspect layout and report remaining overflow
    App->>Render: render Mermaid SVGs, theme CSS, Markdown, and PDF in staging
    App->>Tx: commit manifest with parent revision
    Tx-->>App: immutable child revision and current pointer
    App-->>Client: EditSlidesResult with changed slides, artifacts, warnings, and provenance

    Note over Deck,Agent: Frontmatter, title slide, slide IDs, order, and unrelated content are code-protected.
